Chapter 9
About three thousand years after the Ark's launch, a data retrieval request was initiated from the Memory Sector. The requester was a young astronomer from the Continuation Sector, compiling a list of "bypassed galaxies." During the construction, thousands of galaxies had been removed from the dismantling sequence for various reasons. S7 was one of them.
She pulled up S7's survey file and saw Gu Lin's note. Then she did the calculations.
When the Ark launched, S7 was about three hundred million light-years from the edge of the Mother Membrane. The Mother Membrane disintegration shockwave propagated at the intra-membrane speed of light. S7 would be engulfed by the shockwave about three hundred million years after the Mother Membrane disintegrated. That civilization still had three hundred million years.
She did not know whether to feel comfort or sorrow at that number. Three hundred million years—longer than the entire span from the ignition of the first stars in the Mother Membrane to the Ark's launch. That civilization had enough time to develop, flourish, explore the universe—if they discovered the terminal data.
But she knew S7 was the only exception. She accessed Shen Yuan's file and saw the handwritten note on KD-9A901's dismantling directive—"seven confirmed intelligent civilizations." She saw the unsent letter Shen Yuan had written to Gu Lin.
At the end of her report, she wrote: "Gu Lin bypassed one galaxy. Shen Yuan signed over three hundred extermination directives. We dismantled twelve thousand galaxies in the Mother Membrane and bypassed only one. On a cosmic scale of random distribution, this proportion holds no statistical significance. But on a human scale, it means someone once sat before the star chart for a long time, and then chose to spare one. One. Among all 120 million 'Horizon' files, only one does not conclude with 'terminated.'"
